:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-surface.nse-application-menu .nse-application-menu-list > .nse-menu-separator {
  height: 0;
  margin: 0;
  background: transparent;
  box-shadow: none;
}

:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-surface.nse-application-menu .nse-application-menu-list > .nse-control-list-item:first-of-type {
  border-top-width: 0;
  box-shadow: none;
}

:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-surface.nse-application-menu .nse-application-menu-list > .nse-control-list-item:last-of-type {
  border-bottom-width: 0;
}

/* Row colour, held one notch above the geometry rule above and away from the
   disabled rule below.

   atmo-controls.css writes these rows as `.nse-control-app-menu-inner > *` —
   (0,1,0), a TIE with `.nse-control-list-item` — so the later app-menu rule wins on
   order and the rows read white on the dark system menu. This file's
   `[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-list-item` is (0,2,0) and broke that tie,
   so the colour was restated at (0,2,0) and won back on order. Then the metal
   fix split row colour out into
   `[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-list-item:not([data-nse-material="metal"] *)`.
   `:not()` carries the weight of its argument, so that rule is (0,3,0) — it
   outranks the restatement outright and took the app menu with it. Enabled rows
   went #333 on a #4a4b4c panel; the DISABLED row, at (0,3,0) and later, kept
   #8c8c8c and so read BRIGHTER than the live commands; hover, at (0,4,0), still
   painted white, so the text appeared only under the pointer.
   Now (0,4,0) — surface + inner + :not() — so it wins on weight, not on order.
   See probe-app-menu-popup-text.mjs: nothing in this toolchain scores type. */
:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-surface .nse-control-app-menu-inner > *:not(.is-disabled) {
  color: #fff;
}

/* Restated here because the vector row sets its own `padding: 10px` at (0,2,0),
   which ties atmo-controls.css's app-menu padding and wins on import order —
   rows would keep their labels but lose the 20px that keeps the plate full
   width. (0,3,0) settles it on weight. */
:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-surface .nse-control-app-menu-inner > * {
  padding-right: 20px;
  padding-left: 20px;
}

:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-surface.nse-application-menu .nse-control-app-menu-inner > .nse-menu {
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  padding: 0;
  border: 0;
  border-radius: 0;
  background: transparent;
}

:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-inner > *:first-child {
  border-top-width: 0;
  box-shadow: none;
}

:scope[data-nse-theme="com.syndromatic.atmo"] .nse-control-app-menu-inner > *.is-disabled {
